---

Notes live in the swarm folder, so each device sees the same files. Open
**Notes** in the app to write and edit them; the same files are at
`<mount>/Swarm/Notes` and over WebDAV, and any text editor can open them.

# [Write and edit]($heading.id('writing'))

A new note is a Markdown file named after its title, such as
`Notes/Shopping list.md`. Existing `.txt` notes keep working, and the ones this
device wrote under the old `2026-10-28 17-49-03 …` names are renamed to their
title. The title is the file name: change it in the editor and the file is
renamed. Two notes can't share a title in a notebook.

The editor saves a draft on this device as you type and sends the note to the
swarm a couple of seconds after you stop, when you leave it, when the window is
hidden and on Ctrl+S. The line under the title tells you: "Saving…", "Saved on
this device · syncing" or "Not saved: …" with the reason. A note is only
editable once its text was loaded; if the devices that have it are offline you
see "Can't open" and **Retry**, never an empty note.

Notebooks are folders under `Notes/`. Use **Move to notebook…** with a new name
to make one; a notebook with no notes in it is gone. **Pin** keeps a note at the
top of this device's list; pins are not shared with your other devices. Delete
removes a note at once with an undo for ten seconds.

Search looks at titles as you type, then at the text of the notes this device
has.

| Keys | |
| :--- | :--- |
| Ctrl+N | New note |
| Ctrl+F or Ctrl+K | Search |
| Ctrl+S | Save now |
| Ctrl+E | Preview or edit |
| Ctrl+Shift+P | Pin or unpin |
| Esc | Leave the editor (narrow window) or clear the search |
| Up, Down, Enter | Move through the list and open a note |

# [Markdown]($heading.id('markdown'))

The preview shows headings, paragraphs, bold, italic, strikethrough, inline code
and code blocks, links, bullet, numbered and task lists, quotes and rules.
Nothing else is interpreted: HTML is shown as the text it is, and images are not
loaded. Tick a task box in the preview and the line in the note changes.

# [Share notes]($heading.id('sharing'))

Where the system has a share sheet (Android, Windows, macOS), **Share** sends
the note's text to another app. Everywhere, **Copy text**, **Export…** (a save
dialog) and **Copy link** are in the note's menu. A `nomadfs://note/…` link
opens that note in NomadFS on any device of the swarm. On Linux there is no
system share sheet, so Share is hidden.

Share text or a text file to NomadFS from another app ("Save to NomadFS notes")
and it becomes a note: the subject, or the first line, is the title. If the node
isn't running yet, the note waits and is written when it starts.

**Open by code** (the menu next to the search field) opens any text file of the
swarm by its CID, read only, with a button to save it as a note.

# [Conflicts]($heading.id('conflicts'))

If another device saved the note while you were editing it, nothing is
overwritten. The editor says who changed it and offers three choices: **See
their version** (your text waits behind **Restore my draft** until you leave the
note), **Keep both** (yours is saved as `<title> (from <this device>)`) and
**Replace with mine**, the one choice that discards their version. If you
haven't typed anything, a change from another device just reloads the note.

If two devices edit while they can't reach each other, the swarm keeps both: the
newer edit stays at the note's name and the other becomes `<title> (conflict
from <device>)`. The list shows that copy under its note with a **Conflict**
tag, and **Merge into note** shows both side by side with **Use this one**,
**Append to the note** and **Delete this copy**.

One race is not resolved for you: renaming a note on one device while another
device edits it leaves the note under both names. Delete the one you don't need.
